@@ -3,3 +3,13 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value that a JSON
+Pointer refers to. The empty pointer returns the whole document. It throws an `Error` when the pointer
+is malformed (no leading `/`, or a `~` not followed by `0` or `1`) or does not resolve: missing member,
+array index out of range or with leading zeros, the `-` end-of-array token, or descent into a scalar.
+Only own members are looked up, so `__proto__` or `toString` never resolve.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18 or later, which runs the TypeScript tests directly).
